Pre-release audit (langertha-release-checker) after a171067. Commit 971e750 "fix: k270 review, probe hardening and tolerant id matching" (no karr suffix in the subject, but its body covers ModelProbe/Capabilities work) landed three user-visible robustness changes to probe_model_capabilities_f that the consolidated image_input bullet in Changes (top of {{$NEXT}}) does not mention:

1. ModelProbe->lookup_ids: tolerant id matching - an Ollama id probed as "llama3:latest" now also answers for "llama3" (implicit :latest), and an OpenRouter ":variant" suffix matches its base id.
2. Role/Capabilities.pm: a partial Ollama /api/show 404 for one model in a models=>"all" sweep now skips just that model and keeps the rest, instead of failing the whole probe.
3. local $@ around the chat_model eval in supports() so a caller´s own $@ survives a supports() call.

The Changes bullet says only "probe_model_capabilities_f ... reads image_input per model from the providers own metadata" - accurate but silent on the tolerant-matching and partial-failure behavior a caller can actually observe (e.g. probing by tagged id vs base id, or one bad model id no longer poisoning an "all" sweep).

Fix: add one clause to the existing image_input bullet (or a short follow-on sentence) naming tolerant id matching (Ollama :latest, OpenRouter :variant) and partial-failure tolerance on models=>"all". langertha-pod-writer lane. Non-blocking.
